WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.982
Hoping to do a lot of work this week.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.351
Some people are coming to help.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.686
So pointing the walls...

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:02.355
We'll probably do that in a few days.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:05.358
And in between,
we'll also do some digging work.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.862
I think the excavator is being delivered.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.965
End of the afternoon

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.700
or tomorrow afternoon. We’ll see

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.703
And already start
digging out the hillside.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:21.975
And then dig trenches around, for drainage.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:25.979
Because, as you can see, there's a bit of
water coming through the concrete.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:30.550
It's not really leaking, like concrete
is waterproof,

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.753
but it's not completely impermeable.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.221
It's like a porous material.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:40.860
So if water sits against it,
the concrete gets wet

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:43.663
and that comes through the floor.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:46.666
So it needs a barrier.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.636
It's probably easier
to explain it in a drawing.

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:54.607
And then there's also the same thing
I have to do on the second cabin.

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:58.645
And I have to dig trenches to the battery
box for extra power to the workshop

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.814
and, split it up

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.817
because it's too much to do in one time.

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:08.555
It would be a big mess.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.590
So just do the digging here.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.425
Maybe the trenches to the battery box

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:16.462
But not all around the second cabin

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:34.047
A quick drawing

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:36.683
So water that comes down the hill here

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:40.053
kind of pulls up here, and it can’t go away
quick enough.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:45.225
So it sits in the soil
and it sits against concrete.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:48.228
So the concrete sucks it up, basically.

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:50.763
So I'll put a drainage pipe here

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:53.766
in the ground and dig it out all around.

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:56.903
And a drainage pipe
sits all around the cabin

00:03:56.903 --> 00:04:00.473
so water can go through
the pipe down hill,

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:06.879
and probably the rain gutter pipe that will be on the back will also be connected to this.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:13.086
So water can stream down to...
for the moment it'll come out of the hill

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.287
here.

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:20.560
But eventually
I'll connect everything together also with the system for the second cabin.

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:24.764
For the other side....

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:27.767
So from the top, it will look like this.

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:31.271
This is downhill.

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.472
These are the two cabins.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:33.373
This is the workshop.

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:36.409
So the pipe sits in the ground around it.

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:39.612
So it will go around the corner

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:42.382
stream downhill from there 

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:45.051
